{"parentUuid":"44c6ea2e-b1cb-49a9-8dd0-cd2cff078007","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa6bbad74ebe17310","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffpVtWNyvUvhh4RcbohM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y9SDRypPH5NrBgky3WJ9dv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus_round2.md","content":"# Review round 2: Supertraining Chapter 6, sections 6.4 to 6.8.2 (Ch6b)\n\nReviewer: Claude Opus, independent round-2 falsification pass, 2026-10-03. I did not write or fix these entries.\nScope: the 16 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt`.\nInputs: round-1 review `staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus.md`, fix log `staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6b_applied.md`.\nSource: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx = printed + 11.\n\n## Method\n\n- Text layer (PyMuPDF) for PDF 259-260, 305, 327, 334-336, 347-362, 370-373, 375 and 381, saved to `staging/_tmp/r2_6b_text.json`.\n- A script pulled every double-quoted string out of the 16 entries and matched it against the normalised text. Each miss was then fuzzy-matched by hand. Every source quote is in the source. The misses were OCR noise (\"arc\" for \"are\", \"modem\" for \"modern\", \"changcs\", \"o f\"), figure labels, baseline quotes and quote-pairing artefacts.\n- Page images opened (110 dpi full page unless noted): PDF 348 (Fig 6.12), 351 (plus a 300 dpi crop of Fig 6.15), 353, 358 (plus a **400 dpi crop of Fig 6.22**), 360, 361 (Fig 6.23) and 371. Renders are `staging/_renders/r2_6b_*.png`.\n- Section locations from the text-layer headings: 5.3.3 opens on PDF 303, and 5.4 starts lower on PDF 305, *after* the 23-25%, 4-8 week, 1-3 week and 4-12 week sentences. 6.12.2 opens on PDF 379, with no new heading before PDF 381. 6.7 opens on PDF 356, 6.8.1 on PDF 357, 6.9.5 on PDF 370 (PDF 371 still belongs to it), and 6.2.2 on PDF 334.\n- All 19 cited `docs/method-baseline.md` lines (27, 30, 32, 59, 64, 75, 101, 105, 106, 115, 116, 117, 123, 151, 153, 171, 183, 185, 204): the quotes and tags match, including line 105's \"Not claimed in the interview\".\n- Vault files checked: the Issurin 2016 brief (`research-papers/`) and `periodization--bompa/principle--progressive-overload-threshold`.\n\n## Mechanical checks (all 16 files)\n\n- Six section headers in the vault form (`**X** —`): 16 of 16.\n- Em dashes outside the headers: 0 in every file.\n- Wrapped wikilinks: 0.\n- Process or review-history wording (batch, round, prior version, corrected, fixer, NO-GO, \"text layer only\"): 0 matches.\n- Wikilinks: all 66 unique targets resolve in the staging library or the vault.\n\n## Fig 6.22 graph A (PDF 358 / p.347, 400 dpi crop)\n\nI read graph A, the thick \"Fitness state\" line, myself. On the displayed crop it starts at about y = 445 px, sits at about 265 px at the Year 1/2 boundary and about 150 px at the Year 2/3 boundary, and ends at about 95 px. That is a rise of about 180, 115 and 55 px in Years 1, 2 and 3: a clearly decelerating (concave) curve, and no peak is drawn. The new wording is correct in both entries: \"whose slope shrinks each year (steepest in Year 1, flattest in Year 3)\", \"Graph A flattens year by year\", and \"Graph A's slope shrinks each year ... no peak is drawn\". The rest of the description also matches the image. B and C oscillate around A and dip near each year boundary. D (\"Skill\") is the lower, slowly rising wavy line. The axis is labelled \"RELATIVE LEVELS\" and has no numbers.\n\n## Entries\n\n| File | Verdict | Problem, or what was checked | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| framework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions | GO | Both fixes landed. Fig 6.12 image (PDF 348 / p.337): the shaded band A holds Training Load, Training Potential of Loading and Athlete's Fitness State; region B is the right-hand column (Fitness State, Training Effect, External Interactions). They overlap at fitness state, as the entry now says. The \"only route ... need measuring\" sentence is now labelled Inference. Also checked: \"The basis for the training effect is the accumulation of adaptive traces\" (PDF 348), \"Sports results are the observable product\" (PDF 347, \"arc\" in the text layer), and the subsystem A/B text and \"lower the measures for the first one (A)\" (PDF 348 image). | None required. Optional: the Why it works lead cites PDF 348 for both the one-way chain and the two levels. The chain quote is on PDF 347 and the two levels are on PDF 348, so \"(PDF pp. 347-348)\" would be exact. |\n| heuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity | GO | Both fixes landed. Fig 6.15 at 300 dpi (PDF 351 / p.340): B branches off the right-hand slope of the broad curve and rises to a hump. A and C are separate narrow spikes at low and high arousal. The new description is correct. The note that the personality difference has no source and is hedged (\"appears\") matches the page: no citation is attached to \"the introvert appears to have a lower optimal arousal zone\". All the point 1-5 quotes match the image. | None. |\n| heuristic--build-training-theory-from-interacting-complexes-and-coach-scientist-cooperation | GO (not re-reviewed) | Unchanged since round 1. Its quotes passed the text-layer match (\"specd\" and \"unction\" are OCR noise). The Fig 6.13 box names were image-checked in round 1. Mechanics pass. | None. |\n| heuristic--expectancy-motivation-break-distant-goals-into-attainable-steps | GO (spot-checked) | **Checked against the PDF 353 / p.342 image:** \"Vroom's *Expectancy Theory of Motivation*\", \"(Tellier, 1978)\", the V and B bullets, \"arithmetic product F = V X B\", the -5 to +5 and 0 to 1 scales, which the page attributes to \"Vroom's detailed theory\" (so the entry's \"Vroom's as reported\" is right), \"the sum of the motivational forces\", \"outside the scope of this book\", the break-down-the-goal sentence and the manager/leader sentence. Baseline line 171 (Inferred (transcript)) matches. | None. |\n| framework--situational-leadership-coach-matches-style-to-athlete-maturity | GO (not re-reviewed) | Unchanged. The \"Hersey and Blanchard stated ...\" and \"rates the maturity ... (M1, M2, M3 or M4)\" quotes are in the PDF 354 text layer. Baseline line 204 matches. | None. |\n| framework--three-sport-groups-acyclic-cyclic-complex-for-programming | GO | The fix landed. In the PDF 357 text, \"One should further subdivide the sports in each of these broad groups\" (offset 1122) comes after the cyclic paragraph (470) and before \"Finally, one should identify a third group\" (1617). So the call covers the acyclic and cyclic groups only. The entry now says that, and labels the extension to the complex group as its own inference. Also checked: \"mixed aerobic-anaerobic character, with the greater part being derived from glycolytic reactions\" (PDF 357), and baseline lines 115, 116 and 117, with quotes and tags matching. | None. |\n| principle--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors | **FIX** | Fixes 1 and 2 landed. Why it works now gives \"modern sporting requirements\" and \"common sense\" as the stated basis and labels the weeks-long-effects reasoning Inference. The batch sentence is gone, and the 6.2 link is present. **New problem from the fix:** When NOT says \"the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit\" without a label. PDF 327 / p.316 does call the session one of the \"basic structural units ... (the fundamental unit)\", so \"structural\" is the book's word. But the book never calls the mesocycle a \"planning unit\". PDF 358 says only that \"the fundamental unit of training should be the mesocycle\". That characterisation is the writer's, written as plain text. | Change \"...(PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347); the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit. Inference: the book does not reconcile the wording\" to \"...(PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347). Inference: the first is one of the book's 'structural units', the second reads as a planning unit; the book does not reconcile the wording\". |\n| claim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation | GO | All three fixes landed. Fig 6.22 is described correctly (see the reading above), \"nearly straight\" and \"Figure against text\" are gone, and the PDF 359 locators now read \"checked against the page image\". The folded-in monitoring limit quote (\"in the ability to observe it in the factors used for analysis\"; \"The measures of aerobic and anaerobic output ... do not express the internal changes associated with adaptation to intense cyclic or acyclic work\") is in the PDF 359 text, and the reading that follows is labelled Inference. The four conclusions match the PDF 358 image word for word. | None. |\n| claim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation | GO | All three fixes landed. \"has to be taken much further in its application to the development of sporting mastery, especially in endurance sports\" is now about research (Folbrot, Selye), as on PDF 359. The \"nearly straight\" clause and the \"text layer only\" sentence are gone. The new \"Graph A's slope shrinks each year ... no peak is drawn\" agrees with the 400 dpi crop. \"steadily\" was removed from the Example. All quotes pass the text-layer match (\"cffcct\" and \"o f\" are OCR noise). | None. |\n| principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window | GO (spot-checked) | **Checked against the PDF 360 / p.349 image:** \"acquisition, preservation and brief loss of sporting form (Matveyev, 1964)\", \"effective when it produces the maximum growth of the body's CAR by means of the appropriate volume of loading\", \"means of assessing the body's CAR in each case, together with criteria for determining the contents and volume\", and \"(Beckman et al, 1961; Yakovlev, 1977)\". Letunov 1952, Prokor 1959, \"re-adaptation\" and \"highest sport\" work capacity are in the PDF 359-360 text. The fixer's new Bompa wording (\"an increasing, varied load, adaptation; an unchanging load, plateau; an excessive one, maladaptation\") matches vault `periodization--bompa/principle--progressive-overload-threshold` line 16. Baseline line 75 matches. The new link to `principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue` resolves. | None. |\n| framework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation | GO | All three fixes landed. **(1) Fig 6.23** (PDF 361 image): the dashed lines are at weeks 6 and 12, the x-axis ends at 18 weeks, Panel B's curves recover to 100% around weeks 7-9, and no 3-4 week blocks or 7-10 day pauses are drawn. The new sentence is correct, and \"concentrated in the first half of the training phase\" is on the PDF 360 image. **(2) Issurin 2016:** named as \"the evidence for Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model\", which matches the vault brief line 51 (\"the concentrated-unidirectional (CU) model is Verkhoshansky's; the multi-targeted model ... is Issurin's own A-T-R\"). The p.6 claims (insufficient for combat, team-sport and swimming; fitness gains without reported practice or competition effects) match brief lines 46 and 48, and the p.11 narrow-target-quality claim matches line 50. **(3) PDF 371:** \"Research indicates that both methods are successful in training athletes of medium qualification\" is verbatim on the image (printed p.360). The text layer has \"arc\". The reciprocal link resolves. The When to apply wording was revised to match and is correct. `contested` is justified by Issurin. | None. Trivial: Panel B lows are given as \"around weeks 4-6\", against round 1's \"weeks 4-5\". On the 110 dpi image the troughs sit near weeks 4-5. Either is within reading error. |\n| heuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery | **FIX** | Most of the fix is right on the pages. \"3-4 weeks\", with the optimum \"determined\" (PDF 360 image: \"the optimal duration of the training influences was determined\"); \"for instance, ... 4-8 week concentrated blocks\" (PDF 305, in 5.3.3); \"limited period (of up to 2 months)\" (PDF 381, in 6.12.2); the 4-12 week stage at PDF 305 and 381; the 4-12 week LDTE and \"approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage\" (PDF 375); the 1-3 week latency (PDF 305); and 18-22 weeks (PDF 360 image). The new 23-25% Inference is correctly located: \"23-25% of the general volume for the year\" is in 5.3.3 on PDF 305, before the 5.4 heading, and \"23-25% of the general annual volume\" is in 6.12.2 on PDF 381. It is labelled Inference. The time-limits link resolves. **Error in the new conflict sentence:** \"The 4-8 weeks and 'up to 2 months' agree with each other; the 3-4 weeks overlaps them only at 4 weeks, so the conflict is between the 3-4 week figure and the longer blocks.\" The \"only at 4 weeks\" part is false for \"up to 2 months\". That figure is a ceiling (the same paragraph says it \"reads as a ceiling\"), and 3-4 weeks lies inside it. So the conflict on the pages is 3-4 weeks (PDF 360) against 4-8 weeks (PDF 305) only. `contested` still holds on that pair. | Replace the sentence with: \"The 4-8 weeks and 'up to 2 months' agree with each other. 3-4 weeks lies within the 'up to 2 months' ceiling and meets the 4-8 week range only at 4 weeks, so the conflict is between the 3-4 week figure given as the determined optimum (PDF 360) and the 4-8 week blocks (PDF 305).\" |\n| heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance | GO (spot-checked) | **Checked against the PDF 361 / p.350 image:** the full restorative-stage quote, word for word. \"after the volume of loading is decreased, their increase accelerates\" is on the PDF 360 image. The 1-3 week latency after 4-8 week blocks is in 5.3.3 (PDF 305 text, before the 5.4 heading). The 7-10 day pause and the longer recuperation are on the PDF 360 image. The fixed pointer now reads \"as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]\" and resolves. Baseline line 151 matches. | None. |\n| claim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect | GO | Both fixes landed. The batch sentence is gone and \"Inference:\" now opens Why it works. The full quote is on the PDF 361 image. **On the fixer's Disagreement 3** (\"nothing for either is on 336\"): only half right. The 6.2.2 heading is on PDF 334 and Table 6.1 (reference and caption) is on PDF 335, but 6.2.2 continues on PDF 336, with \"number of lifts in certain intensity zones (% of 1 RM)\" and a mean-intensity table (\"it furnishes upper limits of the mean intensity\"). No new section heading appears until after PDF 339. The entry's \"intensity-zone material ... at PDF pp. 334-335\" is incomplete but not wrong about what it names. | Recommended, not required: \"The 6.2.2 intensity-zone material (PDF pp. 334-336 / printed pp. 323-325) and Table 6.1 (PDF p. 335 / printed p. 324)\". |\n| principle--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system | **FIX** | Both fixes landed. The Zhurbinoi citation now closes the second sentence, as on PDF 362, and the Chapter 4 pointer is labelled Inference. **Error in the fix:** \"the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only\". PDF 362 has three cross-references: \"(see 2.2.3, 5.4.3)\", \"the classification scheme of 6.5\", and \"(... as detailed in 2.2.3)\". The entry itself quotes the 6.5 reference two paragraphs earlier. | Change to: \"the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3, 5.4.3 and '6.5' (the classification scheme, which is in 6.7); none is to Chapter 4.\" |\n| claim--sprint-and-distance-training-emphasis-shifts-with-qualification-vankov | GO | The fix landed. The title now reads \"for Distance Athletes the Top-Level Emphasis Is Printed as Anaerobic\". The When NOT note says \"distance athletes\", not runners, which matches PDF 362. The Vankov quote passes the text-layer match. Baseline line 101 matches. | None. |\n\nCounts: **GO 13, FIX 3, NO-GO 0.**\n\nAll 11 round-1 FIX rows are resolved. The three remaining FIX rows are one-sentence errors that the round-1 fixes introduced (mesocycle, concentrated-blocks, functional-specialisation). None changes a confidence rating.\n\n## Fixer disagreements, judged against the pages\n\n1. **Narrower block-length conflict:** the fixer's claim is justified. 4-8 weeks (PDF 305, \"for instance\") and \"up to 2 months\" (PDF 381, a ceiling) do not conflict, and the real tension is the PDF 360 \"determined\" 3-4 weeks against the PDF 305 4-8 weeks. But the entry sentence that implements it misstates the overlap with \"up to 2 months\" (FIX above).\n2. **PDF 375 ties the LDTE to stage duration:** justified. \"In principle, the duration of the LDTE (T2) is approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage (T1)\", followed by \"the LDTE was observed to last from 4-12 weeks during the long-term stages of strength preparation\" (PDF 375 text).\n3. **Bondarchuk range 334-335 rather than 334-336:** partly justified. The heading and Table 6.1 are on 334-335, but the 6.2.2 intensity material continues on 336 (see the Bondarchuk row).\n4. **Fig 6.22:** agreed. My independent crop confirms the curve decelerates.\n5. **Optional items not applied** (Tellier provenance note, situational \"Inference:\" prefix, Eysenck citation): acceptable, since round 1 marked them optional.\n\n## GO entries spot-checked against the page\n\n- `heuristic--expectancy-motivation-break-distant-goals-into-attainable-steps`: PDF 353 image.\n- `principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window`: PDF 360 image, PDF 359-360 text, and the vault Bompa file.\n- `heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance`: PDF 361 and 360 images, PDF 305 text.\n- Text-layer only, for the other two round-1 GO entries: `build-training-theory` (PDF 349-350) and `situational-leadership` (PDF 354). Every quote matched.\n\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Apply these three one-sentence corrections, then promote:\n\n1. `principle--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors`: move \"Inference:\" in front of the structural-unit and planning-unit characterisation.\n2. `heuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery`: correct \"overlaps them only at 4 weeks\". 3-4 weeks lies inside the \"up to 2 months\" ceiling, and the conflict is 3-4 weeks (PDF 360) against 4-8 weeks (PDF 305).\n3. `principle--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system`: the PDF 362 cross-references are 2.2.3, 5.4.3 and \"6.5\", not \"2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only\".\n\nRecommended, not required: the Bondarchuk locator to PDF pp. 334-336, and the logical-scheme chain locator to PDF pp. 347-348. These fixes need no image re-check by a third reviewer. A grep confirming the three new sentences is enough.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2252,"cache_read_input_tokens":156094,"output_tokens":7858,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":343},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2252},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7858,"cache_read_input_tokens":156094,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2252,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Y9SDRypPH5NrBgky3WJ9dv":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus_round2.md","content":"# Review round 2: Supertraining Chapter 6, sections 6.4 to 6.8.2 (Ch6b)\n\nReviewer: Claude Opus, independent round-2 falsification pass, 2026-10-03. I did not write or fix these entries.\nScope: the 16 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt`.\nInputs: round-1 review `staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus.md`, fix log `staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6b_applied.md`.\nSource: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx = printed + 11.\n\n## Method\n\n- Text layer (PyMuPDF) for PDF 259-260, 305, 327, 334-336, 347-362, 370-373, 375 and 381, saved to `staging/_tmp/r2_6b_text.json`.\n- A script pulled every double-quoted string out of the 16 entries and matched it against the normalised text. Each miss was then fuzzy-matched by hand. Every source quote is in the source. The misses were OCR noise (\"arc\" for \"are\", \"modem\" for \"modern\", \"changcs\", \"o f\"), figure labels, baseline quotes and quote-pairing artefacts.\n- Page images opened (110 dpi full page unless noted): PDF 348 (Fig 6.12), 351 (plus a 300 dpi crop of Fig 6.15), 353, 358 (plus a **400 dpi crop of Fig 6.22**), 360, 361 (Fig 6.23) and 371. Renders are `staging/_renders/r2_6b_*.png`.\n- Section locations from the text-layer headings: 5.3.3 opens on PDF 303, and 5.4 starts lower on PDF 305, *after* the 23-25%, 4-8 week, 1-3 week and 4-12 week sentences. 6.12.2 opens on PDF 379, with no new heading before PDF 381. 6.7 opens on PDF 356, 6.8.1 on PDF 357, 6.9.5 on PDF 370 (PDF 371 still belongs to it), and 6.2.2 on PDF 334.\n- All 19 cited `docs/method-baseline.md` lines (27, 30, 32, 59, 64, 75, 101, 105, 106, 115, 116, 117, 123, 151, 153, 171, 183, 185, 204): the quotes and tags match, including line 105's \"Not claimed in the interview\".\n- Vault files checked: the Issurin 2016 brief (`research-papers/`) and `periodization--bompa/principle--progressive-overload-threshold`.\n\n## Mechanical checks (all 16 files)\n\n- Six section headers in the vault form (`**X** —`): 16 of 16.\n- Em dashes outside the headers: 0 in every file.\n- Wrapped wikilinks: 0.\n- Process or review-history wording (batch, round, prior version, corrected, fixer, NO-GO, \"text layer only\"): 0 matches.\n- Wikilinks: all 66 unique targets resolve in the staging library or the vault.\n\n## Fig 6.22 graph A (PDF 358 / p.347, 400 dpi crop)\n\nI read graph A, the thick \"Fitness state\" line, myself. On the displayed crop it starts at about y = 445 px, sits at about 265 px at the Year 1/2 boundary and about 150 px at the Year 2/3 boundary, and ends at about 95 px. That is a rise of about 180, 115 and 55 px in Years 1, 2 and 3: a clearly decelerating (concave) curve, and no peak is drawn. The new wording is correct in both entries: \"whose slope shrinks each year (steepest in Year 1, flattest in Year 3)\", \"Graph A flattens year by year\", and \"Graph A's slope shrinks each year ... no peak is drawn\". The rest of the description also matches the image. B and C oscillate around A and dip near each year boundary. D (\"Skill\") is the lower, slowly rising wavy line. The axis is labelled \"RELATIVE LEVELS\" and has no numbers.\n\n## Entries\n\n| File | Verdict | Problem, or what was checked | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| framework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions | GO | Both fixes landed. Fig 6.12 image (PDF 348 / p.337): the shaded band A holds Training Load, Training Potential of Loading and Athlete's Fitness State; region B is the right-hand column (Fitness State, Training Effect, External Interactions). They overlap at fitness state, as the entry now says. The \"only route ... need measuring\" sentence is now labelled Inference. Also checked: \"The basis for the training effect is the accumulation of adaptive traces\" (PDF 348), \"Sports results are the observable product\" (PDF 347, \"arc\" in the text layer), and the subsystem A/B text and \"lower the measures for the first one (A)\" (PDF 348 image). | None required. Optional: the Why it works lead cites PDF 348 for both the one-way chain and the two levels. The chain quote is on PDF 347 and the two levels are on PDF 348, so \"(PDF pp. 347-348)\" would be exact. |\n| heuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity | GO | Both fixes landed. Fig 6.15 at 300 dpi (PDF 351 / p.340): B branches off the right-hand slope of the broad curve and rises to a hump. A and C are separate narrow spikes at low and high arousal. The new description is correct. The note that the personality difference has no source and is hedged (\"appears\") matches the page: no citation is attached to \"the introvert appears to have a lower optimal arousal zone\". All the point 1-5 quotes match the image. | None. |\n| heuristic--build-training-theory-from-interacting-complexes-and-coach-scientist-cooperation | GO (not re-reviewed) | Unchanged since round 1. Its quotes passed the text-layer match (\"specd\" and \"unction\" are OCR noise). The Fig 6.13 box names were image-checked in round 1. Mechanics pass. | None. |\n| heuristic--expectancy-motivation-break-distant-goals-into-attainable-steps | GO (spot-checked) | **Checked against the PDF 353 / p.342 image:** \"Vroom's *Expectancy Theory of Motivation*\", \"(Tellier, 1978)\", the V and B bullets, \"arithmetic product F = V X B\", the -5 to +5 and 0 to 1 scales, which the page attributes to \"Vroom's detailed theory\" (so the entry's \"Vroom's as reported\" is right), \"the sum of the motivational forces\", \"outside the scope of this book\", the break-down-the-goal sentence and the manager/leader sentence. Baseline line 171 (Inferred (transcript)) matches. | None. |\n| framework--situational-leadership-coach-matches-style-to-athlete-maturity | GO (not re-reviewed) | Unchanged. The \"Hersey and Blanchard stated ...\" and \"rates the maturity ... (M1, M2, M3 or M4)\" quotes are in the PDF 354 text layer. Baseline line 204 matches. | None. |\n| framework--three-sport-groups-acyclic-cyclic-complex-for-programming | GO | The fix landed. In the PDF 357 text, \"One should further subdivide the sports in each of these broad groups\" (offset 1122) comes after the cyclic paragraph (470) and before \"Finally, one should identify a third group\" (1617). So the call covers the acyclic and cyclic groups only. The entry now says that, and labels the extension to the complex group as its own inference. Also checked: \"mixed aerobic-anaerobic character, with the greater part being derived from glycolytic reactions\" (PDF 357), and baseline lines 115, 116 and 117, with quotes and tags matching. | None. |\n| principle--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors | **FIX** | Fixes 1 and 2 landed. Why it works now gives \"modern sporting requirements\" and \"common sense\" as the stated basis and labels the weeks-long-effects reasoning Inference. The batch sentence is gone, and the 6.2 link is present. **New problem from the fix:** When NOT says \"the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit\" without a label. PDF 327 / p.316 does call the session one of the \"basic structural units ... (the fundamental unit)\", so \"structural\" is the book's word. But the book never calls the mesocycle a \"planning unit\". PDF 358 says only that \"the fundamental unit of training should be the mesocycle\". That characterisation is the writer's, written as plain text. | Change \"...(PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347); the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit. Inference: the book does not reconcile the wording\" to \"...(PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347). Inference: the first is one of the book's 'structural units', the second reads as a planning unit; the book does not reconcile the wording\". |\n| claim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation | GO | All three fixes landed. Fig 6.22 is described correctly (see the reading above), \"nearly straight\" and \"Figure against text\" are gone, and the PDF 359 locators now read \"checked against the page image\". The folded-in monitoring limit quote (\"in the ability to observe it in the factors used for analysis\"; \"The measures of aerobic and anaerobic output ... do not express the internal changes associated with adaptation to intense cyclic or acyclic work\") is in the PDF 359 text, and the reading that follows is labelled Inference. The four conclusions match the PDF 358 image word for word. | None. |\n| claim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation | GO | All three fixes landed. \"has to be taken much further in its application to the development of sporting mastery, especially in endurance sports\" is now about research (Folbrot, Selye), as on PDF 359. The \"nearly straight\" clause and the \"text layer only\" sentence are gone. The new \"Graph A's slope shrinks each year ... no peak is drawn\" agrees with the 400 dpi crop. \"steadily\" was removed from the Example. All quotes pass the text-layer match (\"cffcct\" and \"o f\" are OCR noise). | None. |\n| principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window | GO (spot-checked) | **Checked against the PDF 360 / p.349 image:** \"acquisition, preservation and brief loss of sporting form (Matveyev, 1964)\", \"effective when it produces the maximum growth of the body's CAR by means of the appropriate volume of loading\", \"means of assessing the body's CAR in each case, together with criteria for determining the contents and volume\", and \"(Beckman et al, 1961; Yakovlev, 1977)\". Letunov 1952, Prokor 1959, \"re-adaptation\" and \"highest sport\" work capacity are in the PDF 359-360 text. The fixer's new Bompa wording (\"an increasing, varied load, adaptation; an unchanging load, plateau; an excessive one, maladaptation\") matches vault `periodization--bompa/principle--progressive-overload-threshold` line 16. Baseline line 75 matches. The new link to `principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue` resolves. | None. |\n| framework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation | GO | All three fixes landed. **(1) Fig 6.23** (PDF 361 image): the dashed lines are at weeks 6 and 12, the x-axis ends at 18 weeks, Panel B's curves recover to 100% around weeks 7-9, and no 3-4 week blocks or 7-10 day pauses are drawn. The new sentence is correct, and \"concentrated in the first half of the training phase\" is on the PDF 360 image. **(2) Issurin 2016:** named as \"the evidence for Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model\", which matches the vault brief line 51 (\"the concentrated-unidirectional (CU) model is Verkhoshansky's; the multi-targeted model ... is Issurin's own A-T-R\"). The p.6 claims (insufficient for combat, team-sport and swimming; fitness gains without reported practice or competition effects) match brief lines 46 and 48, and the p.11 narrow-target-quality claim matches line 50. **(3) PDF 371:** \"Research indicates that both methods are successful in training athletes of medium qualification\" is verbatim on the image (printed p.360). The text layer has \"arc\". The reciprocal link resolves. The When to apply wording was revised to match and is correct. `contested` is justified by Issurin. | None. Trivial: Panel B lows are given as \"around weeks 4-6\", against round 1's \"weeks 4-5\". On the 110 dpi image the troughs sit near weeks 4-5. Either is within reading error. |\n| heuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery | **FIX** | Most of the fix is right on the pages. \"3-4 weeks\", with the optimum \"determined\" (PDF 360 image: \"the optimal duration of the training influences was determined\"); \"for instance, ... 4-8 week concentrated blocks\" (PDF 305, in 5.3.3); \"limited period (of up to 2 months)\" (PDF 381, in 6.12.2); the 4-12 week stage at PDF 305 and 381; the 4-12 week LDTE and \"approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage\" (PDF 375); the 1-3 week latency (PDF 305); and 18-22 weeks (PDF 360 image). The new 23-25% Inference is correctly located: \"23-25% of the general volume for the year\" is in 5.3.3 on PDF 305, before the 5.4 heading, and \"23-25% of the general annual volume\" is in 6.12.2 on PDF 381. It is labelled Inference. The time-limits link resolves. **Error in the new conflict sentence:** \"The 4-8 weeks and 'up to 2 months' agree with each other; the 3-4 weeks overlaps them only at 4 weeks, so the conflict is between the 3-4 week figure and the longer blocks.\" The \"only at 4 weeks\" part is false for \"up to 2 months\". That figure is a ceiling (the same paragraph says it \"reads as a ceiling\"), and 3-4 weeks lies inside it. So the conflict on the pages is 3-4 weeks (PDF 360) against 4-8 weeks (PDF 305) only. `contested` still holds on that pair. | Replace the sentence with: \"The 4-8 weeks and 'up to 2 months' agree with each other. 3-4 weeks lies within the 'up to 2 months' ceiling and meets the 4-8 week range only at 4 weeks, so the conflict is between the 3-4 week figure given as the determined optimum (PDF 360) and the 4-8 week blocks (PDF 305).\" |\n| heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance | GO (spot-checked) | **Checked against the PDF 361 / p.350 image:** the full restorative-stage quote, word for word. \"after the volume of loading is decreased, their increase accelerates\" is on the PDF 360 image. The 1-3 week latency after 4-8 week blocks is in 5.3.3 (PDF 305 text, before the 5.4 heading). The 7-10 day pause and the longer recuperation are on the PDF 360 image. The fixed pointer now reads \"as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]\" and resolves. Baseline line 151 matches. | None. |\n| claim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect | GO | Both fixes landed. The batch sentence is gone and \"Inference:\" now opens Why it works. The full quote is on the PDF 361 image. **On the fixer's Disagreement 3** (\"nothing for either is on 336\"): only half right. The 6.2.2 heading is on PDF 334 and Table 6.1 (reference and caption) is on PDF 335, but 6.2.2 continues on PDF 336, with \"number of lifts in certain intensity zones (% of 1 RM)\" and a mean-intensity table (\"it furnishes upper limits of the mean intensity\"). No new section heading appears until after PDF 339. The entry's \"intensity-zone material ... at PDF pp. 334-335\" is incomplete but not wrong about what it names. | Recommended, not required: \"The 6.2.2 intensity-zone material (PDF pp. 334-336 / printed pp. 323-325) and Table 6.1 (PDF p. 335 / printed p. 324)\". |\n| principle--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system | **FIX** | Both fixes landed. The Zhurbinoi citation now closes the second sentence, as on PDF 362, and the Chapter 4 pointer is labelled Inference. **Error in the fix:** \"the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only\". PDF 362 has three cross-references: \"(see 2.2.3, 5.4.3)\", \"the classification scheme of 6.5\", and \"(... as detailed in 2.2.3)\". The entry itself quotes the 6.5 reference two paragraphs earlier. | Change to: \"the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3, 5.4.3 and '6.5' (the classification scheme, which is in 6.7); none is to Chapter 4.\" |\n| claim--sprint-and-distance-training-emphasis-shifts-with-qualification-vankov | GO | The fix landed. The title now reads \"for Distance Athletes the Top-Level Emphasis Is Printed as Anaerobic\". The When NOT note says \"distance athletes\", not runners, which matches PDF 362. The Vankov quote passes the text-layer match. Baseline line 101 matches. | None. |\n\nCounts: **GO 13, FIX 3, NO-GO 0.**\n\nAll 11 round-1 FIX rows are resolved. The three remaining FIX rows are one-sentence errors that the round-1 fixes introduced (mesocycle, concentrated-blocks, functional-specialisation). None changes a confidence rating.\n\n## Fixer disagreements, judged against the pages\n\n1. **Narrower block-length conflict:** the fixer's claim is justified. 4-8 weeks (PDF 305, \"for instance\") and \"up to 2 months\" (PDF 381, a ceiling) do not conflict, and the real tension is the PDF 360 \"determined\" 3-4 weeks against the PDF 305 4-8 weeks. But the entry sentence that implements it misstates the overlap with \"up to 2 months\" (FIX above).\n2. **PDF 375 ties the LDTE to stage duration:** justified. \"In principle, the duration of the LDTE (T2) is approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage (T1)\", followed by \"the LDTE was observed to last from 4-12 weeks during the long-term stages of strength preparation\" (PDF 375 text).\n3. **Bondarchuk range 334-335 rather than 334-336:** partly justified. The heading and Table 6.1 are on 334-335, but the 6.2.2 intensity material continues on 336 (see the Bondarchuk row).\n4. **Fig 6.22:** agreed. My independent crop confirms the curve decelerates.\n5. **Optional items not applied** (Tellier provenance note, situational \"Inference:\" prefix, Eysenck citation): acceptable, since round 1 marked them optional.\n\n## GO entries spot-checked against the page\n\n- `heuristic--expectancy-motivation-break-distant-goals-into-attainable-steps`: PDF 353 image.\n- `principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window`: PDF 360 image, PDF 359-360 text, and the vault Bompa file.\n- `heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance`: PDF 361 and 360 images, PDF 305 text.\n- Text-layer only, for the other two round-1 GO entries: `build-training-theory` (PDF 349-350) and `situational-leadership` (PDF 354). Every quote matched.\n\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Apply these three one-sentence corrections, then promote:\n\n1. `principle--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors`: move \"Inference:\" in front of the structural-unit and planning-unit characterisation.\n2. `heuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery`: correct \"overlaps them only at 4 weeks\". 3-4 weeks lies inside the \"up to 2 months\" ceiling, and the conflict is 3-4 weeks (PDF 360) against 4-8 weeks (PDF 305).\n3. `principle--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system`: the PDF 362 cross-references are 2.2.3, 5.4.3 and \"6.5\", not \"2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only\".\n\nRecommended, not required: the Bondarchuk locator to PDF pp. 334-336, and the logical-scheme chain locator to PDF pp. 347-348. These fixes need no image re-check by a third reviewer. A grep confirming the three new sentences is enough.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffpVnP2Ftgh3xummJesM","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f97d0ab-3e45-4392-a2cd-009cc32b31f4","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:01:56.995Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"5f97d0ab-3e45-4392-a2cd-009cc32b31f4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a651eb06-5033-46b7-b765-1ac5222002ab","agentId":"aa6bbad74ebe17310","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y9SDRypPH5NrBgky3WJ9dv","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus_round2.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"4d88ccf1-e52e-4e09-bc6c-16ed7e94977a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:01:57.430Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus_round2.md","content":"# Review round 2: Supertraining Chapter 6, sections 6.4 to 6.8.2 (Ch6b)\n\nReviewer: Claude Opus, independent round-2 falsification pass, 2026-10-03. I did not write or fix these entries.\nScope: the 16 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt`.\nInputs: round-1 review `staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus.md`, fix log `staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6b_applied.md`.\nSource: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx = printed + 11.\n\n## Method\n\n- Text layer (PyMuPDF) for PDF 259-260, 305, 327, 334-336, 347-362, 370-373, 375 and 381, saved to `staging/_tmp/r2_6b_text.json`.\n- A script pulled every double-quoted string out of the 16 entries and matched it against the normalised text. Each miss was then fuzzy-matched by hand. Every source quote is in the source. The misses were OCR noise (\"arc\" for \"are\", \"modem\" for \"modern\", \"changcs\", \"o f\"), figure labels, baseline quotes and quote-pairing artefacts.\n- Page images opened (110 dpi full page unless noted): PDF 348 (Fig 6.12), 351 (plus a 300 dpi crop of Fig 6.15), 353, 358 (plus a **400 dpi crop of Fig 6.22**), 360, 361 (Fig 6.23) and 371. Renders are `staging/_renders/r2_6b_*.png`.\n- Section locations from the text-layer headings: 5.3.3 opens on PDF 303, and 5.4 starts lower on PDF 305, *after* the 23-25%, 4-8 week, 1-3 week and 4-12 week sentences. 6.12.2 opens on PDF 379, with no new heading before PDF 381. 6.7 opens on PDF 356, 6.8.1 on PDF 357, 6.9.5 on PDF 370 (PDF 371 still belongs to it), and 6.2.2 on PDF 334.\n- All 19 cited `docs/method-baseline.md` lines (27, 30, 32, 59, 64, 75, 101, 105, 106, 115, 116, 117, 123, 151, 153, 171, 183, 185, 204): the quotes and tags match, including line 105's \"Not claimed in the interview\".\n- Vault files checked: the Issurin 2016 brief (`research-papers/`) and `periodization--bompa/principle--progressive-overload-threshold`.\n\n## Mechanical checks (all 16 files)\n\n- Six section headers in the vault form (`**X** —`): 16 of 16.\n- Em dashes outside the headers: 0 in every file.\n- Wrapped wikilinks: 0.\n- Process or review-history wording (batch, round, prior version, corrected, fixer, NO-GO, \"text layer only\"): 0 matches.\n- Wikilinks: all 66 unique targets resolve in the staging library or the vault.\n\n## Fig 6.22 graph A (PDF 358 / p.347, 400 dpi crop)\n\nI read graph A, the thick \"Fitness state\" line, myself. On the displayed crop it starts at about y = 445 px, sits at about 265 px at the Year 1/2 boundary and about 150 px at the Year 2/3 boundary, and ends at about 95 px. That is a rise of about 180, 115 and 55 px in Years 1, 2 and 3: a clearly decelerating (concave) curve, and no peak is drawn. The new wording is correct in both entries: \"whose slope shrinks each year (steepest in Year 1, flattest in Year 3)\", \"Graph A flattens year by year\", and \"Graph A's slope shrinks each year ... no peak is drawn\". The rest of the description also matches the image. B and C oscillate around A and dip near each year boundary. D (\"Skill\") is the lower, slowly rising wavy line. The axis is labelled \"RELATIVE LEVELS\" and has no numbers.\n\n## Entries\n\n| File | Verdict | Problem, or what was checked | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| framework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions | GO | Both fixes landed. Fig 6.12 image (PDF 348 / p.337): the shaded band A holds Training Load, Training Potential of Loading and Athlete's Fitness State; region B is the right-hand column (Fitness State, Training Effect, External Interactions). They overlap at fitness state, as the entry now says. The \"only route ... need measuring\" sentence is now labelled Inference. Also checked: \"The basis for the training effect is the accumulation of adaptive traces\" (PDF 348), \"Sports results are the observable product\" (PDF 347, \"arc\" in the text layer), and the subsystem A/B text and \"lower the measures for the first one (A)\" (PDF 348 image). | None required. Optional: the Why it works lead cites PDF 348 for both the one-way chain and the two levels. The chain quote is on PDF 347 and the two levels are on PDF 348, so \"(PDF pp. 347-348)\" would be exact. |\n| heuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity | GO | Both fixes landed. Fig 6.15 at 300 dpi (PDF 351 / p.340): B branches off the right-hand slope of the broad curve and rises to a hump. A and C are separate narrow spikes at low and high arousal. The new description is correct. The note that the personality difference has no source and is hedged (\"appears\") matches the page: no citation is attached to \"the introvert appears to have a lower optimal arousal zone\". All the point 1-5 quotes match the image. | None. |\n| heuristic--build-training-theory-from-interacting-complexes-and-coach-scientist-cooperation | GO (not re-reviewed) | Unchanged since round 1. Its quotes passed the text-layer match (\"specd\" and \"unction\" are OCR noise). The Fig 6.13 box names were image-checked in round 1. Mechanics pass. | None. |\n| heuristic--expectancy-motivation-break-distant-goals-into-attainable-steps | GO (spot-checked) | **Checked against the PDF 353 / p.342 image:** \"Vroom's *Expectancy Theory of Motivation*\", \"(Tellier, 1978)\", the V and B bullets, \"arithmetic product F = V X B\", the -5 to +5 and 0 to 1 scales, which the page attributes to \"Vroom's detailed theory\" (so the entry's \"Vroom's as reported\" is right), \"the sum of the motivational forces\", \"outside the scope of this book\", the break-down-the-goal sentence and the manager/leader sentence. Baseline line 171 (Inferred (transcript)) matches. | None. |\n| framework--situational-leadership-coach-matches-style-to-athlete-maturity | GO (not re-reviewed) | Unchanged. The \"Hersey and Blanchard stated ...\" and \"rates the maturity ... (M1, M2, M3 or M4)\" quotes are in the PDF 354 text layer. Baseline line 204 matches. | None. |\n| framework--three-sport-groups-acyclic-cyclic-complex-for-programming | GO | The fix landed. In the PDF 357 text, \"One should further subdivide the sports in each of these broad groups\" (offset 1122) comes after the cyclic paragraph (470) and before \"Finally, one should identify a third group\" (1617). So the call covers the acyclic and cyclic groups only. The entry now says that, and labels the extension to the complex group as its own inference. Also checked: \"mixed aerobic-anaerobic character, with the greater part being derived from glycolytic reactions\" (PDF 357), and baseline lines 115, 116 and 117, with quotes and tags matching. | None. |\n| principle--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors | **FIX** | Fixes 1 and 2 landed. Why it works now gives \"modern sporting requirements\" and \"common sense\" as the stated basis and labels the weeks-long-effects reasoning Inference. The batch sentence is gone, and the 6.2 link is present. **New problem from the fix:** When NOT says \"the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit\" without a label. PDF 327 / p.316 does call the session one of the \"basic structural units ... (the fundamental unit)\", so \"structural\" is the book's word. But the book never calls the mesocycle a \"planning unit\". PDF 358 says only that \"the fundamental unit of training should be the mesocycle\". That characterisation is the writer's, written as plain text. | Change \"...(PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347); the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit. Inference: the book does not reconcile the wording\" to \"...(PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347). Inference: the first is one of the book's 'structural units', the second reads as a planning unit; the book does not reconcile the wording\". |\n| claim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation | GO | All three fixes landed. Fig 6.22 is described correctly (see the reading above), \"nearly straight\" and \"Figure against text\" are gone, and the PDF 359 locators now read \"checked against the page image\". The folded-in monitoring limit quote (\"in the ability to observe it in the factors used for analysis\"; \"The measures of aerobic and anaerobic output ... do not express the internal changes associated with adaptation to intense cyclic or acyclic work\") is in the PDF 359 text, and the reading that follows is labelled Inference. The four conclusions match the PDF 358 image word for word. | None. |\n| claim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation | GO | All three fixes landed. \"has to be taken much further in its application to the development of sporting mastery, especially in endurance sports\" is now about research (Folbrot, Selye), as on PDF 359. The \"nearly straight\" clause and the \"text layer only\" sentence are gone. The new \"Graph A's slope shrinks each year ... no peak is drawn\" agrees with the 400 dpi crop. \"steadily\" was removed from the Example. All quotes pass the text-layer match (\"cffcct\" and \"o f\" are OCR noise). | None. |\n| principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window | GO (spot-checked) | **Checked against the PDF 360 / p.349 image:** \"acquisition, preservation and brief loss of sporting form (Matveyev, 1964)\", \"effective when it produces the maximum growth of the body's CAR by means of the appropriate volume of loading\", \"means of assessing the body's CAR in each case, together with criteria for determining the contents and volume\", and \"(Beckman et al, 1961; Yakovlev, 1977)\". Letunov 1952, Prokor 1959, \"re-adaptation\" and \"highest sport\" work capacity are in the PDF 359-360 text. The fixer's new Bompa wording (\"an increasing, varied load, adaptation; an unchanging load, plateau; an excessive one, maladaptation\") matches vault `periodization--bompa/principle--progressive-overload-threshold` line 16. Baseline line 75 matches. The new link to `principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue` resolves. | None. |\n| framework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation | GO | All three fixes landed. **(1) Fig 6.23** (PDF 361 image): the dashed lines are at weeks 6 and 12, the x-axis ends at 18 weeks, Panel B's curves recover to 100% around weeks 7-9, and no 3-4 week blocks or 7-10 day pauses are drawn. The new sentence is correct, and \"concentrated in the first half of the training phase\" is on the PDF 360 image. **(2) Issurin 2016:** named as \"the evidence for Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model\", which matches the vault brief line 51 (\"the concentrated-unidirectional (CU) model is Verkhoshansky's; the multi-targeted model ... is Issurin's own A-T-R\"). The p.6 claims (insufficient for combat, team-sport and swimming; fitness gains without reported practice or competition effects) match brief lines 46 and 48, and the p.11 narrow-target-quality claim matches line 50. **(3) PDF 371:** \"Research indicates that both methods are successful in training athletes of medium qualification\" is verbatim on the image (printed p.360). The text layer has \"arc\". The reciprocal link resolves. The When to apply wording was revised to match and is correct. `contested` is justified by Issurin. | None. Trivial: Panel B lows are given as \"around weeks 4-6\", against round 1's \"weeks 4-5\". On the 110 dpi image the troughs sit near weeks 4-5. Either is within reading error. |\n| heuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery | **FIX** | Most of the fix is right on the pages. \"3-4 weeks\", with the optimum \"determined\" (PDF 360 image: \"the optimal duration of the training influences was determined\"); \"for instance, ... 4-8 week concentrated blocks\" (PDF 305, in 5.3.3); \"limited period (of up to 2 months)\" (PDF 381, in 6.12.2); the 4-12 week stage at PDF 305 and 381; the 4-12 week LDTE and \"approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage\" (PDF 375); the 1-3 week latency (PDF 305); and 18-22 weeks (PDF 360 image). The new 23-25% Inference is correctly located: \"23-25% of the general volume for the year\" is in 5.3.3 on PDF 305, before the 5.4 heading, and \"23-25% of the general annual volume\" is in 6.12.2 on PDF 381. It is labelled Inference. The time-limits link resolves. **Error in the new conflict sentence:** \"The 4-8 weeks and 'up to 2 months' agree with each other; the 3-4 weeks overlaps them only at 4 weeks, so the conflict is between the 3-4 week figure and the longer blocks.\" The \"only at 4 weeks\" part is false for \"up to 2 months\". That figure is a ceiling (the same paragraph says it \"reads as a ceiling\"), and 3-4 weeks lies inside it. So the conflict on the pages is 3-4 weeks (PDF 360) against 4-8 weeks (PDF 305) only. `contested` still holds on that pair. | Replace the sentence with: \"The 4-8 weeks and 'up to 2 months' agree with each other. 3-4 weeks lies within the 'up to 2 months' ceiling and meets the 4-8 week range only at 4 weeks, so the conflict is between the 3-4 week figure given as the determined optimum (PDF 360) and the 4-8 week blocks (PDF 305).\" |\n| heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance | GO (spot-checked) | **Checked against the PDF 361 / p.350 image:** the full restorative-stage quote, word for word. \"after the volume of loading is decreased, their increase accelerates\" is on the PDF 360 image. The 1-3 week latency after 4-8 week blocks is in 5.3.3 (PDF 305 text, before the 5.4 heading). The 7-10 day pause and the longer recuperation are on the PDF 360 image. The fixed pointer now reads \"as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]\" and resolves. Baseline line 151 matches. | None. |\n| claim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect | GO | Both fixes landed. The batch sentence is gone and \"Inference:\" now opens Why it works. The full quote is on the PDF 361 image. **On the fixer's Disagreement 3** (\"nothing for either is on 336\"): only half right. The 6.2.2 heading is on PDF 334 and Table 6.1 (reference and caption) is on PDF 335, but 6.2.2 continues on PDF 336, with \"number of lifts in certain intensity zones (% of 1 RM)\" and a mean-intensity table (\"it furnishes upper limits of the mean intensity\"). No new section heading appears until after PDF 339. The entry's \"intensity-zone material ... at PDF pp. 334-335\" is incomplete but not wrong about what it names. | Recommended, not required: \"The 6.2.2 intensity-zone material (PDF pp. 334-336 / printed pp. 323-325) and Table 6.1 (PDF p. 335 / printed p. 324)\". |\n| principle--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system | **FIX** | Both fixes landed. The Zhurbinoi citation now closes the second sentence, as on PDF 362, and the Chapter 4 pointer is labelled Inference. **Error in the fix:** \"the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only\". PDF 362 has three cross-references: \"(see 2.2.3, 5.4.3)\", \"the classification scheme of 6.5\", and \"(... as detailed in 2.2.3)\". The entry itself quotes the 6.5 reference two paragraphs earlier. | Change to: \"the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3, 5.4.3 and '6.5' (the classification scheme, which is in 6.7); none is to Chapter 4.\" |\n| claim--sprint-and-distance-training-emphasis-shifts-with-qualification-vankov | GO | The fix landed. The title now reads \"for Distance Athletes the Top-Level Emphasis Is Printed as Anaerobic\". The When NOT note says \"distance athletes\", not runners, which matches PDF 362. The Vankov quote passes the text-layer match. Baseline line 101 matches. | None. |\n\nCounts: **GO 13, FIX 3, NO-GO 0.**\n\nAll 11 round-1 FIX rows are resolved. The three remaining FIX rows are one-sentence errors that the round-1 fixes introduced (mesocycle, concentrated-blocks, functional-specialisation). None changes a confidence rating.\n\n## Fixer disagreements, judged against the pages\n\n1. **Narrower block-length conflict:** the fixer's claim is justified. 4-8 weeks (PDF 305, \"for instance\") and \"up to 2 months\" (PDF 381, a ceiling) do not conflict, and the real tension is the PDF 360 \"determined\" 3-4 weeks against the PDF 305 4-8 weeks. But the entry sentence that implements it misstates the overlap with \"up to 2 months\" (FIX above).\n2. **PDF 375 ties the LDTE to stage duration:** justified. \"In principle, the duration of the LDTE (T2) is approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage (T1)\", followed by \"the LDTE was observed to last from 4-12 weeks during the long-term stages of strength preparation\" (PDF 375 text).\n3. **Bondarchuk range 334-335 rather than 334-336:** partly justified. The heading and Table 6.1 are on 334-335, but the 6.2.2 intensity material continues on 336 (see the Bondarchuk row).\n4. **Fig 6.22:** agreed. My independent crop confirms the curve decelerates.\n5. **Optional items not applied** (Tellier provenance note, situational \"Inference:\" prefix, Eysenck citation): acceptable, since round 1 marked them optional.\n\n## GO entries spot-checked against the page\n\n- `heuristic--expectancy-motivation-break-distant-goals-into-attainable-steps`: PDF 353 image.\n- `principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window`: PDF 360 image, PDF 359-360 text, and the vault Bompa file.\n- `heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance`: PDF 361 and 360 images, PDF 305 text.\n- Text-layer only, for the other two round-1 GO entries: `build-training-theory` (PDF 349-350) and `situational-leadership` (PDF 354). Every quote matched.\n\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Apply these three one-sentence corrections, then promote:\n\n1. `principle--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors`: move \"Inference:\" in front of the structural-unit and planning-unit characterisation.\n2. `heuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery`: correct \"overlaps them only at 4 weeks\". 3-4 weeks lies inside the \"up to 2 months\" ceiling, and the conflict is 3-4 weeks (PDF 360) against 4-8 weeks (PDF 305).\n3. `principle--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system`: the PDF 362 cross-references are 2.2.3, 5.4.3 and \"6.5\", not \"2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only\".\n\nRecommended, not required: the Bondarchuk locator to PDF pp. 334-336, and the logical-scheme chain locator to PDF pp. 347-348. These fixes need no image re-check by a third reviewer. A grep confirming the three new sentences is enough.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5f97d0ab-3e45-4392-a2cd-009cc32b31f4","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
